          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Empress of India</strong><br>\nIn 1876, Victoria was given the title Empress of India, reflecting the British Empire's expansion under her reign, which by then included India, Australia, Canada, and much of Africa.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years</strong><br>\nVictoria's Golden and Diamond Jubilees, marking 50 and 60 years on the throne, were celebrated with great fanfare and enthusiasm by the public.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nQueen Victoria died on January 22, 1901. Her 63-year reign was the longest of any British monarch until that point and influenced the transition of Britain into a modern constitutional monarchy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
